/-!
# Generating families

A real function `S(q, a)` on a product `V × A` of normed spaces, the *auxiliary variables* `a`
ranging over `A`, is a **generating family**. Its *fibre derivative* is

`∂_a S : V × A → A'`, `(q, a) ↦ D S(q, a) (0, ·)`

(`TauCeti.cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv`), and its *fibre-critical set* is the zero set
`Σ_S = {(q, a) | ∂_a S(q, a) = 0}`. The source projection
`ι_S (q, a) = (q, ∂_q S(q, a))` of the cotangent relation generated by `S`
(`TauCeti.cotangentGeneratingSource`) maps `Σ_S` to the linear cotangent space `V × V'`. With the
convention `λ_(q,p)(δq, δp) = p(δq)` and `ω = -dλ` of `TauCeti.cotangentLiouvilleForm` and
`TauCeti.strongDualCotangentSymplecticForm`, this file proves the three facts making `ι_S` on
`Σ_S` an exact Lagrangian:

* **Exactness.** At a fibre-critical point the Liouville form pulls back along `ι_S` to `dS`,
  because there `dS(δq, δa) = ∂_q S(δq)`
  (`TauCeti.cotangentLiouvilleForm_compContinuousLinearMap_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource`).
* **Isotropy.** Where the second derivative of `S` is symmetric, the derivative of `ι_S` sends
  the kernel of the derivative of `∂_a S` to an isotropic subspace
  (`TauCeti.strongDualCotangentSymplecticForm_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_eq_zero`).
* **Injectivity.** If moreover that derivative `D(∂_a S)` is surjective, the generating family
  is *transverse* at the point, and the derivative of `ι_S` is injective on its kernel
  (`TauCeti.injOn_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_ker`).

When `V` and `A` are finite-dimensional the kernel of a surjective `D(∂_a S)` has the dimension
of `V`, so its image is a Lagrangian subspace of `V × V'`
(`TauCeti.isLagrangian_map_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_ker`).

Globally, if `S` is smooth and transverse along `Σ_S`, the fibre-critical set is a regular level
set of `∂_a S` of index `dim V`. With the atlas of `TauCeti.levelSetChartedSpace`
(`TauCeti.cotangentFamilyCriticalSetChartedSpace`) it is a smooth manifold of dimension `dim V`
(`TauCeti.isManifold_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet`), whose tangent space at a point is the kernel of
`D(∂_a S)` there. Then `ι_S` restricted to `Σ_S` is a Lagrangian immersion into `V × V'`
(`TauCeti.isLagrangianImmersion_cotangentGeneratingSource_comp_coe`), along which the Liouville
form pulls back to the differential of the restriction of `S`
(`TauCeti.cotangentLiouvilleForm_mfderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_comp_coe`). Its image need not
be embedded: distinct critical points with the same image under `ι_S` give self-intersections, so
embeddedness is an additional hypothesis on the family. A first-kind generating function
`S(q, Q)` is the case `A = W` of the auxiliary variables `Q`; its fibre-critical set is the set
where the target covector `P = -∂_Q S` vanishes.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S`: the fibre derivative `∂_a S` of a generating family.
* `TauCeti.cotangentFamilyCriticalSetChartedSpace`: the charted-space structure on the
  fibre-critical set of a smooth transverse generating family.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.isLagrangian_map_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_ker`: at a transverse point, the
  derivative of `ι_S` maps the kernel of `D(∂_a S)` onto a Lagrangian subspace.
* `TauCeti.isManifold_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet`,
  `TauCeti.range_mfderiv_coe_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet`: the fibre-critical set of a smooth
  transverse generating family is a manifold of dimension `dim V`, with tangent spaces the kernels
  of `D(∂_a S)`.
* `TauCeti.isLagrangianImmersion_cotangentGeneratingSource_comp_coe`: the fibre-critical set maps
  to `V × V'` by `ι_S` as a Lagrangian immersion.
* `TauCeti.cotangentLiouvilleForm_mfderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_comp_coe`: this Lagrangian
  immersion is exact, with primitive the restriction of `S`.

## References

* L. Hörmander, *Fourier integral operators. I*, Acta Math. 127 (1971), 79–183, Section 3.1, for
  the Lagrangian defined by a nondegenerate phase function.
* A. Weinstein, *Lectures on Symplectic Manifolds*, CBMS Regional Conference Series in
  Mathematics 29, AMS, 1977, for generating families (Morse families).
-/

public section

open ContinuousLinearMap Module
open scoped Manifold ContDiff

noncomputable section

namespace TauCeti

variable {V A : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup V] [NormedSpace ℝ V] [NormedAddCommGroup A]
  [NormedSpace ℝ A] {S : V × A → ℝ} {x : V × A}

/-! ### The fibre derivative -/

/-- The **fibre derivative** `∂_a S(q, a) = D S(q, a) (0, ·)` of a generating family
`S : V × A → ℝ` in its auxiliary variables `a ∈ A`. -/
def cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv (S : V × A → ℝ) (x : V × A) : StrongDual ℝ A :=
  (fderiv ℝ S x).comp (inr ℝ V A)

@[simp]
theorem cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv_apply (S : V × A → ℝ) (x : V × A) (b : A) :
    cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x b = fderiv ℝ S x (0, b) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The fibre derivative of `S` is the negated covector of the target projection of the cotangent
relation generated by `S`. -/
theorem cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv_eq_neg_cotangentGeneratingTarget_snd (S : V × A → ℝ)
    (x : V × A) : cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = -(cotangentGeneratingTarget S x).2 := by
  ext b
  simp

/-- The fibre derivative, with the restriction of covectors written as a continuous linear map. -/
private theorem cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv_eq_precomp (S : V × A → ℝ) :
    cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S = fun y ↦ precomp ℝ (inr ℝ V A) (fderiv ℝ S y) := by
  funext y
  ext b
  simp

/-- The derivative of the fibre derivative: `δx ↦ D²S δx (0, ·)`. -/
theorem hasFDerivAt_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv (hS : DifferentiableAt ℝ (fderiv ℝ S) x) :
    HasFDerivAt (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S)
      (precomp ℝ (inr ℝ V A) ∘L fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ S) x) x := by
  rw [cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv_eq_precomp]
  exact (precomp ℝ (inr ℝ V A)).hasFDerivAt.comp x hS.hasFDerivAt

@[simp]
theorem fderiv_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv_apply (hS : DifferentiableAt ℝ (fderiv ℝ S) x)
    (u : V × A) :
    fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x u = (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ S) x u).comp (inr ℝ V A) := by
  simp [(hasFDerivAt_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv hS).fderiv]

/-- If `S` is `C^(n+1)` at `x`, its fibre derivative is `C^n` there. -/
theorem contDiffAt_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv {n : WithTop ℕ∞} (hS : ContDiffAt ℝ (n + 1) S x) :
    ContDiffAt ℝ n (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x := by
  rw [cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv_eq_precomp]
  exact (precomp ℝ (inr ℝ V A)).contDiff.contDiffAt.comp x (hS.fderiv_right le_rfl)

/-- The fibre derivative of a `C²` function is strictly differentiable. -/
theorem hasStrictFDerivAt_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv (hS : ContDiffAt ℝ 2 S x) :
    HasStrictFDerivAt (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S)
      (fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x) x :=
  (contDiffAt_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv (n := 1) hS).hasStrictFDerivAt one_ne_zero

/-! ### The linear algebra at one point -/

/-- **Exactness on the fibre-critical set.** At a point where the fibre derivative vanishes, the
Liouville form pulls back along the source projection `ι_S (q, a) = (q, ∂_q S(q, a))` to `dS`:
`∂_q S(δq) = dS(δq, δa)`. -/
theorem cotangentLiouvilleForm_compContinuousLinearMap_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource
    (hS : DifferentiableAt ℝ (fderiv ℝ S) x) (hx : cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0) :
    (cotangentLiouvilleForm (cotangentGeneratingSource S x)).compContinuousLinearMap
        (fderiv ℝ (cotangentGeneratingSource S) x) =
      differentialOneForm S x := by
  -- The target covector `-∂_a S` vanishes, so the target term of the exactness of the generated
  -- relation drops out.
  have hP : (cotangentGeneratingTarget S x).2 = 0 := by
    rw [← neg_eq_zero, ← cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv_eq_neg_cotangentGeneratingTarget_snd, hx]
  rw [← cotangentLiouvilleForm_cotangentGeneratingSource_sub hS, eq_comm, sub_eq_self]
  ext v
  simp [hP]

/-- **Isotropy.** Where the second derivative of `S` is symmetric, the derivative of the source
projection `ι_S` sends two vectors of the kernel of the derivative of `∂_a S` to `ω`-orthogonal
vectors. No transversality is needed. -/
theorem strongDualCotangentSymplecticForm_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_eq_zero
    (hS : DifferentiableAt ℝ (fderiv ℝ S) x) (hsymm : IsSymmSndFDerivAt ℝ S x) {u v : V × A}
    (hu : fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x u = 0)
    (hv : fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x v = 0) :
    strongDualCotangentSymplecticForm (fderiv ℝ (cotangentGeneratingSource S) x u)
      (fderiv ℝ (cotangentGeneratingSource S) x v) = 0 := by
  -- The target projection has derivative `(δq, δa) ↦ (δa, -D(∂_a S) (δq, δa))`, which vanishes
  -- in the covector direction on the kernel.
  rw [strongDualCotangentSymplecticForm_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource hS hsymm,
    fderiv_cotangentGeneratingTarget_apply hS, fderiv_cotangentGeneratingTarget_apply hS]
  rw [fderiv_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv_apply hS] at hu hv
  simp [hu, hv]

/-- At a transverse point, a vector of the kernel of the derivative of `∂_a S` which the
derivative of the source projection kills is zero. -/
private theorem eq_zero_of_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_eq_zero
    (hS : DifferentiableAt ℝ (fderiv ℝ S) x) (hsymm : IsSymmSndFDerivAt ℝ S x)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x)) {u : V × A}
    (hu : fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x u = 0)
    (hιu : fderiv ℝ (cotangentGeneratingSource S) x u = 0) : u = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨a, b⟩ := u
  rw [fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_apply hS, Prod.mk_eq_zero] at hιu
  obtain ⟨rfl, hq⟩ := hιu
  rw [fderiv_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv_apply hS] at hu
  -- `D²S (0, b)` vanishes on both factors, hence everywhere; by symmetry every covector in the
  -- range of `D(∂_a S)`, which is all of `A'`, vanishes on `b`.
  have hH (w : V × A) : fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ S) x (0, b) w = 0 := by
    have h₁ := DFunLike.congr_fun hq w.1
    have h₂ := DFunLike.congr_fun hu w.2
    simp only [comp_apply, inl_apply, inr_apply, zero_apply] at h₁ h₂
    rw [← Prod.fst_add_snd w, map_add, h₁, h₂, add_zero]
  refine Prod.ext rfl (SeparatingDual.eq_zero_of_forall_dual_eq_zero (R := ℝ) fun β ↦ ?_)
  obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := hsurj β
  rw [fderiv_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv_apply hS, comp_apply, inr_apply, ← hsymm, hH]

/-- **Injectivity at a transverse point.** If the second derivative of `S` is symmetric and the
derivative of the fibre derivative `∂_a S` is surjective, the derivative of the source projection
`ι_S` is injective on the kernel of the derivative of `∂_a S`. -/
theorem injOn_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_ker (hS : DifferentiableAt ℝ (fderiv ℝ S) x)
    (hsymm : IsSymmSndFDerivAt ℝ S x)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x)) :
    Set.InjOn (fderiv ℝ (cotangentGeneratingSource S) x)
      (LinearMap.ker (fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x).toLinearMap) := by
  intro u hu v hv huv
  rw [← sub_eq_zero]
  refine eq_zero_of_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_eq_zero hS hsymm hsurj ?_ ?_
  · simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, LinearMap.mem_ker, coe_coe] at hu hv
    rw [map_sub, hu, hv, sub_zero]
  · rw [map_sub, huv, sub_self]

/-- **The tangent Lagrangian of a generating family.** Let `V` and `A` be finite-dimensional. If
the second derivative of `S` is symmetric at `x` and the derivative of the fibre derivative
`∂_a S` is surjective there, then the derivative of the source projection `ι_S` maps the kernel
of the derivative of `∂_a S` onto a Lagrangian subspace of `V × V'`. -/
theorem isLagrangian_map_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_ker [FiniteDimensional ℝ V]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ A] (hS : DifferentiableAt ℝ (fderiv ℝ S) x)
    (hsymm : IsSymmSndFDerivAt ℝ S x)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x)) :
    strongDualCotangentSymplecticForm.IsLagrangian
      ((LinearMap.ker (fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x).toLinearMap).map
        (fderiv ℝ (cotangentGeneratingSource S) x).toLinearMap) := by
  set K := LinearMap.ker (fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x).toLinearMap
  set ι := (fderiv ℝ (cotangentGeneratingSource S) x).toLinearMap
  refine SymplecticForm.IsIsotropic.isLagrangian_of_finrank ?_ ?_
  · rw [SymplecticForm.isIsotropic_iff]
    rintro _ ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩ _ ⟨v, hv, rfl⟩
    exact strongDualCotangentSymplecticForm_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_eq_zero hS hsymm hu hv
  · -- The kernel of the surjection `D(∂_a S) : V × A → A'` has the dimension of `V`, and `ι` is
    -- injective on it.
    have hK : finrank ℝ K = finrank ℝ V := by
      have h := LinearMap.finrank_range_add_finrank_ker
        (fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x).toLinearMap
      rw [LinearMap.range_eq_top.2 hsurj, finrank_top, dual_finrank_eq, finrank_prod] at h
      simp only [K]
      omega
    have hinj : Function.Injective (ι ∘ₗ K.subtype) := fun u v huv ↦
      Subtype.ext (injOn_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_ker hS hsymm hsurj u.2 v.2 huv)
    rw [← Submodule.range_subtype K, ← LinearMap.range_comp, LinearMap.finrank_range_of_inj hinj,
      hK, finrank_prod, dual_finrank_eq]
    ring

/-! ### The fibre-critical set as a manifold -/

section CriticalSet

variable [FiniteDimensional ℝ V] [FiniteDimensional ℝ A]

/-- The derivative of the fibre derivative has Fredholm index `dim V`. -/
private theorem index_fderiv_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv (x : V × A) :
    (fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x).index = finrank ℝ V := by
  rw [index_eq_of_finiteDimensional, finrank_prod, dual_finrank_eq]
  push_cast
  ring

/-- The **fibre-critical set** `{x | ∂_a S x = 0}` of a generating family `S` which is smooth and
transverse along it, as a charted space modelled on `Fin (dim V) → ℝ`: it is a regular level set
of the fibre derivative, with the atlas of `TauCeti.levelSetChartedSpace`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
def cotangentFamilyCriticalSetChartedSpace
    (hS : ∀ x ∈ {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0}, ContDiffAt ℝ ∞ S x)
    (hsurj : ∀ x ∈ {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0},
      Function.Surjective (fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x)) :
    ChartedSpace (Fin (finrank ℝ V) → ℝ) {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0} :=
  levelSetChartedSpace
    (fun x hx ↦ hasStrictFDerivAt_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv ((hS x hx).of_le (by simp)))
    (fun _ _ ↦ isFredholm_of_finiteDimensional _) hsurj
    (fun x _ ↦ index_fderiv_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv x)

variable (hS : ∀ x ∈ {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0}, ContDiffAt ℝ ∞ S x)
  (hsurj : ∀ x ∈ {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0},
    Function.Surjective (fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) x))

/-- The fibre-critical set of a smooth transverse generating family is a smooth manifold of
dimension `dim V`. -/
theorem isManifold_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet :
    letI := cotangentFamilyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hsurj
    IsManifold 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ V) → ℝ) ∞ {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0} :=
  isManifold_levelSet _ _ _ _ fun x hx ↦
    contDiffAt_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv (by simpa using hS x hx)

/-- The inclusion of the fibre-critical set is smooth. -/
theorem contMDiff_coe_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet :
    letI := cotangentFamilyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hsurj
    ContMDiff 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ V) → ℝ) 𝓘(ℝ, V × A) ∞
      (Subtype.val : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → V × A) :=
  contMDiff_coe_levelSet _ _ _ _ fun x hx ↦
    contDiffAt_cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv (by simpa using hS x hx)

/-- The tangent space of the fibre-critical set at `z` is the kernel of the derivative of the
fibre derivative there. -/
theorem range_mfderiv_coe_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet (z : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0}) :
    letI := cotangentFamilyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hsurj
    (mfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ V) → ℝ) 𝓘(ℝ, V × A)
      (Subtype.val : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → V × A) z).range =
      (fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) z.1).ker :=
  range_mfderiv_coe_levelSet _ _ _ _ z

/-- Along the inclusion of the fibre-critical set, the differential of a map which is
differentiable on `V × A` is its Fréchet derivative applied to the differential of the
inclusion. -/
private theorem mfderiv_comp_coe_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet_apply {F : Type*}
    [NormedAddCommGroup F] [NormedSpace ℝ F] {g : V × A → F}
    (z : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0}) (hg : DifferentiableAt ℝ g z.1) :
    letI := cotangentFamilyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hsurj
    ∀ v : TangentSpace 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ V) → ℝ) z, mfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ V) → ℝ) 𝓘(ℝ, F)
        (g ∘ (Subtype.val : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → V × A)) z v =
      fderiv ℝ g z.1 (mfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ V) → ℝ) 𝓘(ℝ, V × A)
        (Subtype.val : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → V × A) z v) := by
  let _ := cotangentFamilyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hsurj
  intro v
  rw [mfderiv_comp_apply z hg.mdifferentiableAt
    ((contMDiff_coe_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet hS hsurj z).mdifferentiableAt (by simp)),
    mfderiv_eq_fderiv]
  simp only [comp_apply, ContinuousLinearEquiv.coe_coe, NormedSpace.fromTangentSpace_apply,
    NormedSpace.fromTangentSpace_symm_apply]
  -- The two sides differ only in whether the vectors are typed in tangent spaces or in the model
  -- spaces, which are the same types.
  rfl

/-- **The fibre-critical set of a generating family is a Lagrangian immersion.** Let `S` be a
generating family on finite-dimensional spaces `V × A`, smooth along its fibre-critical set and
transverse there: the derivative of `∂_a S` is surjective at every point where `∂_a S`
vanishes. With its manifold structure as a regular level set, the fibre-critical set maps to
`V × V'` by `ι_S (q, a) = (q, ∂_q S(q, a))` as a Lagrangian immersion for the canonical symplectic
form. -/
theorem isLagrangianImmersion_cotangentGeneratingSource_comp_coe :
    letI := cotangentFamilyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hsurj
    (SymplecticForm.isNondegenerate_constSmooth
        (strongDualCotangentSymplecticForm (V := V))).IsLagrangianImmersion
      𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ V) → ℝ)
      (cotangentGeneratingSource S ∘
        (Subtype.val : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → V × A)) := by
  let _ := cotangentFamilyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hsurj
  have := isManifold_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet hS hsurj
  have hι (z : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0}) :
      ContDiffAt ℝ ∞ (cotangentGeneratingSource S) z.1 :=
    contDiffAt_cotangentGeneratingSource (by simpa using hS z z.2)
  have hD (z : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0}) :
      DifferentiableAt ℝ (fderiv ℝ S) z.1 :=
    ((hS z z.2).fderiv_right (m := 1) (by simp)).differentiableAt one_ne_zero
  have hsymm (z : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0}) : IsSymmSndFDerivAt ℝ S z.1 :=
    (hS z z.2).isSymmSndFDerivAt (by simp)
  have hmem (z : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0}) (v) :
      mfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ V) → ℝ) 𝓘(ℝ, V × A)
        (Subtype.val : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → V × A) z v ∈
        LinearMap.ker (fderiv ℝ (cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S) z.1).toLinearMap := by
    rw [← range_mfderiv_coe_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet hS hsurj z]
    exact ⟨v, rfl⟩
  have hsmooth : ContMDiff 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ V) → ℝ) 𝓘(ℝ, V × StrongDual ℝ V) ∞
      (cotangentGeneratingSource S ∘
        (Subtype.val : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → V × A)) := fun z ↦
    (hι z).contMDiffAt.comp z (contMDiff_coe_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet hS hsurj z)
  refine ⟨isImmersion_iff_forall_isImmersionAt.2 fun z ↦
    (hsmooth.contMDiffOn.isImmersionAt_iff_injective_mfderiv isOpen_univ (Set.mem_univ z)
      (by simp)).2 ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · -- The inclusion is injective with tangent image the kernel, on which `dι_S` is injective.
    intro v w hvw
    rw [mfderiv_comp_coe_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet_apply hS hsurj z
        ((hι z).differentiableAt (by simp)),
      mfderiv_comp_coe_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet_apply hS hsurj z
        ((hι z).differentiableAt (by simp))] at hvw
    exact injective_mfderiv_coe_levelSet _ _ _ _ z
      (injOn_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_ker (hD z) (hsymm z) (hsurj z z.2) (hmem z v)
        (hmem z w) hvw)
  · rw [SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.isIsotropicMap_iff]
    intro z v w
    rw [SymplecticForm.fromTangentSpace_constSmooth_apply, NormedSpace.fromTangentSpace_apply,
      NormedSpace.fromTangentSpace_apply,
      mfderiv_comp_coe_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet_apply hS hsurj z
        ((hι z).differentiableAt (by simp)),
      mfderiv_comp_coe_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet_apply hS hsurj z
        ((hι z).differentiableAt (by simp))]
    exact strongDualCotangentSymplecticForm_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_eq_zero (hD z)
      (hsymm z) (hmem z v) (hmem z w)
  · simp only [finrank_fin_fun, finrank_prod, dual_finrank_eq]
    ring

/-- **The fibre-critical set is an exact Lagrangian.** Along the inclusion of the fibre-critical
set of a smooth transverse generating family `S`, the Liouville form pulls back by
`ι_S (q, a) = (q, ∂_q S(q, a))` to the differential of the restriction of `S`. -/
theorem cotangentLiouvilleForm_mfderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource_comp_coe
    (z : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0}) :
    letI := cotangentFamilyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hsurj
    ∀ v : TangentSpace 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ V) → ℝ) z,
      cotangentLiouvilleForm (cotangentGeneratingSource S z.1)
        (fun _ ↦ mfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ V) → ℝ) 𝓘(ℝ, V × StrongDual ℝ V)
          (cotangentGeneratingSource S ∘
            (Subtype.val : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → V × A)) z v) =
      mfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ V) → ℝ) 𝓘(ℝ)
        (S ∘ (Subtype.val : {x | cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → V × A)) z v := by
  let _ := cotangentFamilyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hsurj
  have hD : DifferentiableAt ℝ (fderiv ℝ S) z.1 :=
    ((hS z z.2).fderiv_right (m := 1) (by simp)).differentiableAt one_ne_zero
  intro v
  rw [mfderiv_comp_coe_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet_apply hS hsurj z
      ((contDiffAt_cotangentGeneratingSource (n := 1) ((hS z z.2).of_le (by simp))).differentiableAt
        one_ne_zero),
    mfderiv_comp_coe_cotangentFamilyCriticalSet_apply hS hsurj z
      ((hS z z.2).differentiableAt (by simp))]
  exact
    (DFunLike.congr_fun
      (cotangentLiouvilleForm_compContinuousLinearMap_fderiv_cotangentGeneratingSource hD z.2)
      _).trans (differentialOneForm_apply _ _ _)

